# Bottom line

The best high-confidence architecture is:

[
\boxed{
\text{validated/filtered sales}
\rightarrow
\text{fold-specific local time-adjusted target}
\rightarrow
\text{LightGBM on assessment-stage features}
\rightarrow
\text{scaled time-adjusted comparable-sales feature}
\rightarrow
\text{equity-aware calibration}
}
]

The most promising spatial feature is:

[
\boxed{
y_j+\widehat\tau(t_i,t_j)+\hat f_0(X_i)-\hat f_0(X_j)
}
]

averaged over prior nearby comparable sales.

The most important correction to your current code is:

[
\boxed{
\text{remove group filtering if intended, cross-fit residual features, and move from RMSE selection to curve-aware selection.}
}
]

The most important conceptual rule is:

> Use sale-only features to clean or adjust the target, use assessment-stage features to predict market value, use spatial features as fold-safe comparable evidence, and use ratio-curve diagnostics to choose among models.

